Article 1 The People's Courts shall accept the following patent dispute cases:
1. Cases involving disputes over the ownership of patent application rights;
2. Cases involving disputes over the ownership of patent rights;
3. Cases involving patent contract disputes;
4. Cases involving infringement of patent rights;
5. Cases involving counterfeiting another person's patent;
6. Cases involving disputes over royalties for the temporary protection period of invention patents;
7. Cases involving disputes over rewards and remuneration for inventors or designers of service inventions;
8. Cases involving disputes over applications for pre-litigation preservation of conduct;
9. Cases involving disputes over applications for pre-litigation property preservation;
10. Cases involving disputes over liability for damage caused by an application for preservation of conduct;
11. Cases involving disputes over liability for damage caused by an application for property preservation;
12. Cases involving disputes over the right of inventors or designers of inventions to be named;
13. Cases involving disputes over confirmation of non-infringement of patent rights;
14. Cases involving disputes over return of fees after a patent right is declared invalid;
15. Cases involving disputes over liability for damage caused by maliciously bringing a patent infringement lawsuit;
16. Cases involving disputes over royalties for standard essential patents;
17. Cases challenging the review decision of the patent administrative department of the State Council maintaining the rejection of an application;
18. Cases challenging the decision of the patent administrative department of the State Council on a request for invalidation of a patent right;
19. Cases challenging the compulsory licensing decision made by the patent administrative department of the State Council;
20. Cases challenging the adjudication on compulsory licensing fees made by the patent administrative department of the State Council;
21. Cases challenging the administrative reconsideration decision made by the patent administrative department of the State Council;
22. Cases challenging other administrative decisions made by the patent administrative department of the State Council;
23. Cases challenging administrative decisions made by the department administering patent work;
24. Cases involving disputes over confirmation of whether an act falls within the scope of protection of a patent right;
25. Other patent dispute cases.

Article 5 In a case involving infringement of a utility model or design patent right accepted by the People's Court, if the defendant requests, within the defence period, a declaration of invalidity of the patent right, the People's Court shall suspend the action, except that it may not suspend the action under any of the following circumstances:
(1) the search report or patent evaluation report submitted by the plaintiff does not disclose grounds that would lead to the invalidation of the utility model or design patent right;
(2) the evidence submitted by the defendant is sufficient to prove that the technology it uses is already publicly known;
(3) the evidence or grounds provided by the defendant in requesting the declaration of invalidity of the patent right are obviously insufficient; or
(4) other circumstances in which the People's Court considers that the action should not be suspended.
